# Each function runs once, and what it is handed is one of two kinds. A closure in an arm of a test captures the name as the test has left it; one behind the join captures the name as it came.
# They are different values to the plan: each has a word of its own, stored where the name is made, of the type of what is stored there, or it stays a capture. No reader takes another reader's type.
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: abc! 22
# ANSWERS-NEXT: false number
# ANSWERS-NEXT: 5,4 0,0 6,5
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-PromotedEnvironments
# HELD: abc! 22
# HELD-NEXT: false number
# HELD-NEXT: 5,4 0,0 6,5
# RUN(CALLED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining
# CALLED: abc! 22
# CALLED-NEXT: false number
# CALLED-NEXT: 5,4 0,0 6,5
